       "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Enneagram Quiz Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is an enneagram quiz?\", \"a\": \"An enneagram quiz is a short set of questions that maps your answers to one of the Enneagram's nine basic personality types. Shorter versions sort answers into a center first: there are three centers, with three types in each. The quiz on this page plays that center step.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create an enneagram quiz?\", \"a\": \"Describe it in one prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a>: the results you want, how many questions, and what happens when someone finishes. Emergent builds the quiz, the result screens, and the table that stores every answer, and you change any of it by prompting.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I keep an enneagram quiz free for everyone who takes it?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Keep the enneagram quiz free for takers and still request an address before the full result. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many results can an enneagram personality quiz support?\", \"a\": \"Nine, one per type, when the quiz runs about 25 questions; at 9 to 12 questions, aim for a center instead. Each result needs several questions that can point to it, or one stray answer decides it. A <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/hair-type'>hair type quiz</a> picks from far fewer results, and 8 questions can carry it.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should an enneagram type quiz show on the result screen?\", \"a\": \"Show the type, a paragraph on how that lean looks in daily life, and its wings. A wing is one of the two types adjacent to the taker's type on the circle. End with one next step, such as a longer test or a coaching call.\"}, {\"q\": \"How should an enneagram types quiz handle a tie between two types?\", \"a\": \"Ask one tiebreaker question. When two types finish level, show a final question whose options point only to those two. That lets the taker settle it, which is fairer than letting the order of your result list decide.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should a short enneagram quiz sort by center before type?\", \"a\": \"Yes, if it has fewer than about 15 questions. The Body center holds Types 8, 9, and 1; Heart holds 2, 3, and 4; Head holds 5, 6, and 7. A center is a result a short quiz can support. A general <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/personality'>personality quiz</a> has no such grouping to lean on.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I phrase enneagram quiz results so they do not read as a label?\", \"a\": \"Write each result as a lean, such as your answers lean toward Type 4, never as a fixed verdict. A free enneagram quiz describes preferences. Say that in one line on the result screen, and point takers to a longer test for more depth.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should an enneagram quiz show scores for all nine types?\", \"a\": \"Yes, below the main result. Lead with the top type, then list all nine scores in order. A taker whose top two types are close can then read about both. Ask for the breakdown in your prompt, and Emergent builds it as a chart on the result screen.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one app run an enneagram quiz alongside other quizzes?\", \"a\": \"Yes, in an app Emergent builds: one app can hold an enneagram quiz for self-awareness and a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/career'>career quiz</a> for role interests, keyed to the same email address. Emergent builds both from prompts. Data lives in a database the user owns, with both sets of answers side by side.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
      }
     }
    ]
